16 1. First, find the number of guests who will actually attend the party. Since 1/4 of the invited guests don't show up, the number of attending guests is 16 - (1/4 * 16) = 16 - 4 = 12. 2. Next, find the number of gift bags needed. Christina needs 0.75 gift bags per guest, so she needs 0.75 * 12 = 9 gift bags. 3. Finally, calculate the total cost of the gift bags. Each gift bag costs $2, so the total cost is 9 * $2 = $18.

Therefore, Christina will spend $18.
\boxed{18}

