1/4 of the attendees don't show up, so the number of guests that will actually attend the party is 6: 16 * (1 - 1/4) = 6. Christina needs 0.75 gift bags per guest, so the total number of gift bags needed is 6 * 0.75 = 4.5. Since Christina cannot buy half a gift bag, she needs to buy 5 gift bags. Each gift bag costs $2, so the total cost of gift bags is 5 * $2 = $10.
So the answer is 10.
\boxed{10}
